# Q4. Managing Kubernetes with Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)

Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) is a **managed Kubernetes platform** by Microsoft Azure that simplifies cluster setup, scaling, maintenance, and upgrades.

---

## 🛠️ Creating an AKS Cluster

You can create an AKS cluster using Azure CLI:

### ✅ Command:
```bash
az aks create \
  --resource-group myResourceGroup \
  --name myAKSCluster \
  --node-count 2 \
  --enable-addons monitoring \
  --generate-ssh-keys


YAML Example:
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 8080
  initialDelaySeconds: 5
  periodSeconds: 10

Full Snippet:

containers:
- name: my-app
  image: my-app-image
  ports:
  - containerPort: 8080
  livenessProbe:
    httpGet:
      path: /health
      port: 8080
    initialDelaySeconds: 5
    periodSeconds: 10
  readinessProbe:
    httpGet:
      path: /ready
      port: 8080
    initialDelaySeconds: 5
    periodSeconds: 10
